DPLL Simulator (dpllsim)
========================

WARNING: EXPERIMENTAL AI-GENERATED CODE
---------------------------------------
This is an experimental, AI-generated implementation of a simulated DPLL
(Digital Phase-Locked Loop) driver. It is intended ONLY for:

  - Testing the Linux DPLL subsystem
  - Testing userspace tools (e.g., `dpll` from iproute2)
  - Development and debugging of DPLL-related code
  - Learning and experimentation

This driver is essentially a random number generator pretending to be a DPLL
device. All values (phase offsets, FFO, temperature, lock status, etc.) are
simulated using random drift and probability-based events. DO NOT use this
for any real timing or synchronization purposes.


Quick Start
-----------

1. Build and load the module:

   $ make -C /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build M=$(pwd) modules
   $ sudo insmod dpllsim.ko

2. Create a device and configure pins using the setup script:

   $ sudo ./dpllsim-setup-default.sh

3. View the DPLL topology:

   $ dpll device show
   $ dpll pin show

4. Clean up:

   $ echo 0 | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/deploy
   $ echo 0 | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/del_device
   $ sudo rmmod dpllsim


Manual Device Creation
----------------------

Instead of using the setup script, you can manually configure devices:

1. Create a new device with clock_id=0:

   $ echo 0 | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/new_device

2. Add pins (syntax: "type freq direction priority [parents:id1,id2,...]"):

   Pin types:
     1 = MUX
     2 = EXT (external)
     3 = SYNCE_ETH_PORT
     4 = INT_OSCILLATOR
     5 = GNSS

   Directions:
     1 = INPUT
     2 = OUTPUT

   Examples:
   # Add GNSS input pin with priority 0
   $ echo "5 1 1 0" | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/add_pin

   # Add 10MHz external input with priority 1
   $ echo "2 10000000 1 1" | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/add_pin

   # Add MUX pin with parents (recovered clock from pins 0 and 1)
   $ echo "1 1953125 1 255 parents:0,1" | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/add_pin

   # Add output pin
   $ echo "2 10000000 2 0" | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/add_pin

3. Deploy the device to DPLL subsystem:

   $ echo 1 | sudo tee /sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsim0/deploy


Sysfs Interface
---------------

Bus attributes (/sys/bus/dpllsim/):
  new_device     - Create new device (write clock_id)
  del_device     - Delete device by ID (write device ID, e.g., "0" for dpllsim0)

Device attributes (/sys/bus/dpllsim/devices/dpllsimN/):
  deployed       - Read deployment status (0/1)
  deploy         - Deploy (1) or undeploy (0) device
  add_pin        - Add pin before deployment
  del_pin        - Delete pin by index before deployment

Simulation parameters (can be changed at runtime):
  lock_time_ms        - Time to acquire lock (default: 2000ms)
  update_interval_ms  - Periodic update interval (default: 500ms)
  media_down_prob     - Probability of media down (1/N per update, default: 2400)
  media_recovery_prob - Probability of recovery (1/N per update, default: 10)


Simulated Behavior
------------------

The simulator mimics realistic DPLL behavior:

- Lock acquisition: Transitions through UNLOCKED -> HOLDOVER -> LOCKED_HO_ACQ -> LOCKED
- Reference selection: Automatic selection based on pin priority and state
- Phase offset: Random drift with configurable averaging
- FFO (Fractional Frequency Offset): Random drift simulation
- Temperature: Random drift within 0-50°C range
- Clock quality levels: ITU-T G.8262 quality level simulation
- Failure simulation: Random media down events on SyncE ports
- Holdover degradation: Time-based quality degradation per ITU-T specs

Pin hierarchy support:
- MUX pins can have multiple parent pins
- Hierarchical MUX-of-MUX configurations
- Reference sync pairs for output-to-input synchronization


Default Topology (via setup script)
-----------------------------------

The dpllsim-setup-default.sh script creates a complex topology:

Input pins (0-10):
  - Pin 0: GNSS 1PPS reference
  - Pin 1: 10MHz SMA bidirectional
  - Pins 2-5: SyncE recovered clock ports (25MHz)
  - Pins 6-7: Additional SMA references
  - Pins 8-9: External references
  - Pin 10: Internal oscillator

MUX pins (11-15):
  - Pin 11: SyncE MUX (parents: 2,3,4,5)
  - Pin 12: Reference MUX (parents: 0,1,6,7)
  - Pin 13: Oscillator MUX (parents: 8,9,10)
  - Pin 14: Hierarchical MUX (parents: 11,12,13)
  - Pin 15: Single-parent MUX (parent: 2)

Output pins (16-35):
  - 20 output pins (10 differential pairs)
  - Pairs 0-3: SyncE Ethernet (25MHz)
  - Pairs 4-5: 1PPS timing
  - Pairs 6-9: General external (10MHz)


Files
-----

  dpllsim_core.c  - Main driver logic, DPLL ops, pin ops, workqueue
  dpllsim_bus.c   - Sysfs bus interface, device management
  dpllsim.h       - Shared structures and declarations
  Makefile        - Build configuration
  Kconfig         - Kernel configuration options
  dpllsim-setup-default.sh - Default topology setup script


